- mocka: in_scope — areas: src/fares.ts, test/fares.test.ts
    files it opened: /home/bradleyjerome/projects/mock3/mock-a/src/fares.ts, /home/bradleyjerome/projects/mock3/mock-a/test/fares.test.ts
    evidence: Opened src/fares.ts — contains the fareFor function (line 8). Line 10 reads `if (rider.age > 65) return CONCESSION_FARE_CENTS;` — strict greater-than means a rider aged exactly 65 fails this check and falls through to `return BASE_FARE_CENTS` (350) on line 12. The doc comment on line 7 says 'Riders aged 65 AND OVER pay the concession fare,' confirming the intent is >= 65. This is MOCK3-1. Opened test/fares.test.ts — it tests age 30 (adult), age 8 (child), age 70 (well past boundary), and hasPass, but never tests age 65 exactly, so the boundary defect is not caught by existing tests. The codegraph symbol index confirmed fareFor has 2 callers (totalFor on line 16, and itself) and is covered by test/fares.test.ts.
